{"seq":null,"commit_to":{"owner":"pertson-labs","repo":"e2e-expert-repo","branch":"live/first-version--dfb61a7cef6a"},"doc_stem":"2026-07-25-1-e2e-overwrite-1784972849059","status":"completed","machine":{"spec_version":7,"spec_hash":"c834f46b2b0c"},"checkpoint":"navigate","run_id":"mp-eng-0c618b01","payload":{"expand_iris":["ns__Strategy","ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst","ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping"],"focus":"First version document review, reviewer assignment, initial draft submission","rationale":"The document is a minimal stub — a 'First version' note with a reviewer assignment by Xena ExpertGH. The perspective returned only the Strategy area with two decisions (DiagnosticFirst and KnowledgeMapping). I expanded both children of Strategy to give the passes whatever organizational context exists, since the document's 'first version' framing could relate to Xena's diagnostic-first methodology (starting with understanding before solutions). No other areas were surfaced by the perspective, and the document's content is too thin to justify reaching further into the graph.","n8n_execution_id":"135363","expansion_count":3,"context":"# Perspective — pertson-labs/e2e-expert-repo @ 5ff955b9b3791b94f06bbb545e4fabf4b5e83a79\npin: b7f7301b018946be3cac4fc052c2f6ef92e20265\n\nSections, stable-first: (1) THE MAP — the richest areas at steering grain; (2) AREA INDEX — every other area, named, one line each; (3) ACTIVE SURFACE — recent + load-bearing witnesses; (4) FOCUS — material loaded for your focus, LAST. The map and index never vary with your focus; your per-call material is at the end.\n\n^-marked entries are compressed stubs carrying child addresses. Their narration and any surfaced witness quotes are verbatim-accurate — quote them as-is — but a stub carries no provenance (source, date, supersession). Expand (aswritten_expand with the IRIs you need) before any claim that turns on WHEN or by WHOM something was said, or whether it is still the current framing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nDeciding where to go: each mapped area's narration tells you the SPAN of what lives under it; the area index names everything else. Expand a subtree when its narration (or name) shows your subject plausibly lives there — you'll get the trajectory, the variants, and the verbatim witness. But be strict about absence: if neither the map's narrations nor the index's names substantively cover your subject, it is NOT in this perspective — say so rather than expanding a loose thematic match (a word-overlap is not coverage). Decide from the map; expand to ground.\n\n# The map (steering grain)\n\n\n# Focus: First version document review, reviewer assignment, initial draft submission (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n\n### ns__Strategy\n\nchildren (witness depth):\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping\ntype: ns__Decision\nVisualize where decisions happen and where knowledge lives. Deliverable: knowledge gap report with prioritized recommendations.\nKnowledge Gap Mapping\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst  (already in your context)\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping  (already in your context)\n\n\nserved: ^ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst, ^ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping, ^ns__Strategy\n(pass this list back as `have` on your next expand — content you already hold is then returned as a bare ^pointer, never re-sent)","positions":"","pin":"b7f7301b018946be3cac4fc052c2f6ef92e20265","positions